1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,260
Every day, millions of parcels
leave your warehouses.

2
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:10,210
Most hold exactly what
the customer ordered.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,510
Some don't. And the customer only
finds out after the parcel is opened.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,490
Counterfeit and pirated goods worth 467
billion dollars crossed borders in 2021.

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,870
That is 2.3 percent of world imports.

6
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,660
The figure has barely moved in five years.

7
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:39,390
What has changed is how fakes travel.

8
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:45,460
Eight in ten customs seizures
of fakes are now small parcels.

9
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,870
That is what an online order looks like.

10
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,990
Fashion, footwear, watches and
jewellery are hit hardest.

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,390
These are your high-value categories.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,630
Amazon alone spent more than a billion
dollars in 2024 protecting its store.

13
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:09,070
That is only the cost of defence.

14
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:16,494
Then come the returns, the refunds, the
reverse pickups, and the support tickets

15
00:01:16,344 --> 00:01:18,950
where it's one person's
word against another's.

16
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,100
The cost that matters most
is harder to measure.

17
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:29,309
About two in three shoppers say they would
lose trust in a marketplace after buying

18
00:01:29,159 --> 00:01:29,750
a fake.

19
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,780
Run your own numbers.

20
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:39,606
If just one percent of sales on ten billion
dollars are fakes, that could cost about

21
00:01:39,456 --> 00:01:43,170
fifty million dollars a year,
before you count reputation.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,090
TrueChain gives every high-value item
its own record, one you can check.

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,130
The record starts at the factory.

24
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,350
The brand registers the item.

25
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:05,060
Suppliers and assemblers add parts,
inspections and certificates.

26
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:07,870
Distributors and retailers log the sale.

27
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,660
Every entry is signed and dated.

28
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:17,950
It is held on a shared ledger, and a
summary is published each day where no one,

29
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:20,470
including us, can quietly change it.

30
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,850
Anyone can scan a QR code and read
that history, with no sign-in needed.

31
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,490
Your marketplace uses it at three moments.

32
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:45,740
Before listing: if the record isn't found,
or can't be trusted, the listing stops.

33
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:50,590
If the brand has flagged the item as
stolen or recalled, it goes on hold.

34
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:58,255
At the seller: the record shows which retailer
made the first sale, so you can review

35
00:02:58,105 --> 00:02:59,730
sellers who don't match it.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,682
In a dispute: your support team has a
record to look at, not two people arguing

37
00:03:07,532 --> 00:03:08,530
over photos.

38
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,530
The buyer gets a plain answer:

39
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:17,990
record verified, attention needed,
not found, or could not be trusted.

40
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:24,770
We'll be straight with you.

41
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:28,360
TrueChain doesn't promise
that an item is genuine.

42
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:31,880
It proves that a record exists,
and hasn't been altered.

43
00:03:31,890 --> 00:03:35,700
It's only as strong as
the brands that join.

44
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:39,250
And today, it covers the first
retail sale, not resale.

45
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,730
That's why we suggest proving
it together, not on our word.

46
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,040
The value appears in
numbers you already track:

47
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:56,876
fewer disputes over fakes, fewer returns
and refunds, stolen goods held before they

48
00:03:56,726 --> 00:04:01,466
sell, higher conversion on high-value
listings, and better terms with the brands

49
00:04:01,316 --> 00:04:02,250
you want to keep.

50
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,560
Today, TrueChain is in
pilot with luxury watches.

51
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:11,510
Nothing in the design
is limited to watches.

52
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,280
Here's what we propose:

53
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:20,580
two brands, one category, ninety days.

54
00:04:20,590 --> 00:04:24,910
We agree the targets before we start,
then read the results together.

55
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,160
Every item, a record you can check.

56
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:32,770
Let's build trust into every order.

